messages:
ajay.k: Heads up — big bank POC kickoff tomorrow. They want streaming + function-calls + strict structured JSON outputs. Security just dropped a questionnaire, deadline Fri.
maria_sanders: Got it. Which SDK are they planning to use for the demo? Node on the frontend and Python on the backend?
lina_chen: Correct, node demo + python backend. I can paste a minimal Node streaming + functions example that also enforces JSON output schema.
ajay.k: That would be perfect — also need guidance on handling partial JSON chunks when streaming so the demo doesn’t look flaky. :sweat_smile:
lina_chen: Quick example (Node):
```js
const {Client} = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const client = new Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = await client.chat.stream({
  model: 'rw-infer-4x',
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Get account 4321 and return as ACCOUNT_JSON' }],
  functions: [
    {
      name: 'get_account',
      description: 'Return account details as structured JSON',
      parameters: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: { id: { type: 'string' } },
        required: ['id']
      }
    }
  ],
  // optional: request strict schema enforcement if supported by model runtime
  json_schema: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, balance: { type: 'number' } }, required: ['id'] }
});
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  // handle incremental streaming deltas; buffer until a full JSON is detected
  process.stdout.write(chunk.delta);
}
```
Note: for the demo buffer small deltas client-side and validate after close.
maria_sanders: Nice. On the pricing/contract side — they asked whether we can do a 30-day Dedicated trial or credits instead of a reserved commit. What's our usual play?
tom-b: Historically we offer pilot credits for hosted usage (30k-50k) and a short-term Dedicated eval with limited capacity if they commit to a commercial term. Sales can push credits + a timeboxed Dedicated pilot if needed.
maria_sanders: I'll propose a credits-first approach and a follow-up Dedicated eval contingent on SSO/KMS acceptance. I'll draft an addendum template.
replay-bot: security: questionnaire uploaded -> https://files.company.com/bigbank/presales_security_q2026.pdf :lock: (uploaded by scanner-bot)
ajay.k: InfoSec says KMS + SAML SSO are non-negotiable before any production data. Does Hosted support customer-managed KMS and SAML?
lina_chen: Hosted supports customer-managed KMS for key wrapping (via KMS integration), but SAML SSO for console access and API key issuance is enterprise-only and often requires Dedicated or Private for isolated auth flows. We also have a network allowlist option for Dedicated/Private.
ajay.k: Sounds like an enterprise blocker unless they accept a trial with synthetic data. 
maria_sanders: We'll surface the tradeoffs: synthetic-data pilot on Hosted vs Private/Dedicated for live data. I'll put both options in the proposal.
lina_chen: Also flagging one integration gotcha: when using streaming + function calls + structured output, make sure the function / schema sizes are small (<16KB) and test seq lengths — kernel selection affects latency. I can run a quick perf sample for their typical prompt distribution.
ajay.k: Action items: 
- @maria_sanders confirm credits + draft addendum by EOD
- @lina_chen paste full Node gist + perf sample by tomorrow
- @ajay.k schedule InfoSec deep-dive Thurs 11am (invite sent)
maria_sanders: On it. Will include contract language for KMS and SSO options.
ajay.k: Thanks team — I’ll tell the customer we have a path forward (synthetic-hosted pilot or Dedicated eval), and share the streaming snippet in the call. :thumbsup:
